<title>USA: Top Ten Cargo Carriers at JFK/Newark Jan-Sept 96.</title>
<headline>Top Ten Cargo Carriers at JFK/Newark Jan-Sept 96.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Port Authority of New York and New Jersey said American Airlines headed the list of cargo carriers importing and exporting between January - September 1996 from John F. Kennedy and Newark airports.</p>
<p>The top ten cargo airlines, in order according to combined import and export tonnage handled, were;</p>
<p>	    JANUARY - SEPTEMBER 1996</p>
<p>    J.F. KENNEDY		   NEWARK</p>
<p> 1  American Airlines	  1  Federal Express</p>
<p> 2  Lufthansa Cargo	    2  United Parcel Service</p>
<p> 3  Korean Airlines	    3  Continental Airways</p>
<p> 4  United Airlines	    4  Air Bourne</p>
<p> 5  Asiana Airlines	    5  United Air Lines</p>
<p> 6  DHL Worldwide		6  Scandinavia</p>
<p> 7  Trans World Airlines     7  American International Airlines</p>
<p> 8  Polar Airlines	     8  Emery Worldwide</p>
<p> 9  British Airways	    9  Mountain Air</p>
<p> 10 Federal Express	   10  American Airlines</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
</text>
